  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed side dormer, by reason of its scale, siting and design would represent an overly dominant and incongruous form of development that would erode the original appearance of the host property. The scheme would cause less than substantial harm to the CA73 Burlington Avenue & West Park Road Conservation Area of which it forms part, and there are considered to be no public benefits to outweigh this harm. As such, the proposals are found to be contrary to policy, in particular, 28 and 29 of the Richmond Local Plan (2025), Section 72 (1) of the Planning (Listed Buildings and Conservation Areas) Act 1990, Policy HC1 (C) of the London Plan (2021) and the test in paragraphs 212-215 of the NPPF (2024), as supported by the CA73 Burlington Avenue & West Park Road Conservation Area Statement."
